Findings worth keeping for k242 and the hub:
- Baseline probe 43942781724 (old workflow, before any k167 change) failed on two legs: macOS "The configuration 'macos-14-arm64-us-default' is not supported" (runner image retired, macos-15 is the replacement); Windows cpanm "Module 'ExtUtils::MakeMaker' is not installed" (most likely Git Bash's MSYS perl shadows Strawberry on PATH). Both concern our own workflow and go with it.
- TLS: HTTP::Tiny verify_SSL uses IO::Socket::SSL's default CA lookup (SSL_CERT_FILE/SSL_CERT_DIR, then OPENSSLDIR, then Mozilla::CA). Skilletor::Url maps status 599 to "fetch failed", so only a real https url sync proves TLS; a smoke without one proves nothing.
- Stock linkage needs a shared OpenSSL the targets lack: bullseye links OpenSSL 1.1 (absent on Debian 12+, Ubuntu 22.04+, RHEL 9 without compat-openssl11); macOS links the tool cache's dylibs; Strawberry ships libssl-3-x64__.dll, libcrypto-3-x64__.dll and zlib1__.dll and bakes in an OPENSSLDIR under the build path.
- Net::SSLeay against a static OpenSSL 3 (OPENSSLDIR=/etc/ssl), local docker proof of an x86_64 build: rockylinux:9 5/5 pass; debian:12 pass via the Mozilla::CA fallback; ubuntu:22.04 public https works; glibc floor 2.29 by symbol versions; RHEL needs libxcrypt-compat (libcrypt.so.1). This matches the p5-mcp-hub binary_prepare pattern that k242 adopts.

